\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Effective successful support}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{support}

\p{For threshold #{\varepsilon>0}, the \strong{effective successful support}
of #{(\pi,D,b)} on task #{q} is}

##{
  \operatorname{Supp}^{+}_{\varepsilon}(\pi,D,b;q)
  =\{\tau\in\mathcal S^+(q):
      \mathbb P^{D,b}_{q,\pi}(\{\tau\})\geq\varepsilon\}.
}

\p{This is an FTIP proposal built from ordinary probability support and an
explicit finite threshold. The threshold depends on the granularity of the
trajectory representation; exact token traces and strategy classes produce
different sets.}

\p{The object supports finite elicitation tests. A post-trained policy may
increase the probability of an existing member, add a member above threshold,
or succeed through a new strategy class. Each claim requires a declared
equivalence relation on trajectories.}
